{
  "id": "2026-10-08-jpeg-xl-chrome",
  "title": "크롬이 몇 년 만에 JPEG XL 을 다시 지원한다",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Chrome is finally adding support for a photo format called JPEG XL.",
    "It compresses images thirty to fifty percent smaller than regular JPEGs, without losing quality.",
    "Years ago, Chrome quietly dropped support for the format, saying barely anyone was asking for it.",
    "This time, web developers kept requesting it, and a cross-browser testing project pushed Chrome to reconsider.",
    "The new decoder is written in Rust, a language that catches memory bugs before they ship.",
    "That matters because image decoders sit right where browsers handle data from random websites, which makes them a common target for attacks.",
    "Support lands in Chrome 155, and the team says fuzzing and code review turned up zero memory-safety bugs so far.",
    "If you build anything that serves images on the web, it might be worth testing JPEG XL alongside AVIF to see which compresses your photos better."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "크롬이 JPEG XL 이미지 포맷 디코딩을 Chrome 155 부터 다시 지원한다.",
    "몇 년 전 지원을 접었다가, 개발자 요청이 꾸준히 이어지자 되살렸다.",
    "이번엔 러스트로 디코더를 새로 짜서 메모리 안전 버그를 미리 막았다."
  ],
